  'hub.c2b':'Elements Labs products are intended exclusively for scientific laboratory research — in vitro (cell cultures), in vivo (animal models) and mechanistic studies. They are not intended for use in the human body, are not classified as medicinal products and are not suitable for diagnostic or therapeutic purposes.',
  'hub.c3t':'Quality & analytics: COA / HPLC / SDS',
  'hub.c3b':'A Certificate of Analysis (COA) documents identity and purity testing (HPLC: high-performance liquid chromatography; MS: mass spectrometry), endotoxin tests and further specifications per batch. HPLC separates substances by chemical properties and measures purity precisely. An SDS (Safety Data Sheet) contains safety guidance for laboratory handling. All analyses are published only after genuine, independent testing.',
  'hub.c4t':'Legal situation & responsibility',
  'hub.c4b':'The legal classification of research peptides varies by country and substance. The buyer is solely responsible for reviewing national regulations, import rules and ethical requirements. Elements Labs provides no legal advice.',
  'hub.c5t':'Safe handling & storage',
  'hub.c5b':'Store lyophilized peptides at −20 °C, protected from light and dry. Equilibrate to room temperature before opening to avoid condensation. Short-term storage at 4 °C (max. 4 weeks). Wear protective equipment (gloves, safety glasses) during laboratory work. Specific storage and handling requirements are found in the respective COA and SDS.',
